# lattice-frx dependencies (runtime + test), all upstream PyPI.
# Regenerate the lock with `bazel run //:requirements.update`.
#
# numpy backs the host reference ring; frx and zk-dtypes back the device one.
# Neither is a crypto library and neither is a scheme repo — enc-frx and
# sig-frx already sit on both, so depending on them closes no loop (see
# MODULE.bazel). pytest and scipy are test-only; scipy backs the sampler's
# distribution checks (chi-square / Kolmogorov-Smirnov).
#
# frx / frxlib / zk-dtypes move in lockstep: a frx wheel bump that leaves
# zk-dtypes behind fails at the field dtypes rather than at the pin. These are
# the versions sig-frx runs, which is the pair known to agree.
numpy
frx==0.10.2.dev20260812130529
frxlib==0.10.2.dev20260812130529
zk-dtypes==0.0.14
pytest
scipy
